#: atay ([[price]]) → ataye (the price of something)

===Usage notes===
* '''-e''' as an affiliative suffix often appears in words ended with -y or -w. It is also common in words which the last syllabe is CVC (consonant-vowel-consonant) and has '''-e-''' as its {{w|Syllable#Components|nucleus}}.
: kes (the end) → kese (the end of something)
: puy (a hole) → puye (something’s hole)
: ciw (flow) → ciwe (the flow of something)

