Many Hungarian dialects preserve a distinction between two vowels that are both written with ''e'' and are pronounced {{IPAchar|/ɛ/}} in the standard language. In text that wishes to highlight the distinction, ''e'' ("open e") is contrasted with {{m|hu|ë}} ("closed e").

