====Usage notes====
* In monosyllables, final ⟨{{l|frr||e}}⟩ is pronounced {{IPAchar|[e]}}, except on Sylt, where it is {{IPAchar|[ɛ]}}.
* The reduced vowel is lowered to {{IPAchar|[ɐ]}} when followed by [[coda]] ⟨{{l|frr|r}}⟩. In the insular dialects, the same usually happens also before any other coda consonant (except ⟨{{l|frr|[[l]], [[n]]}}⟩, which become [[syllabic]] instead).
* Mooring Frisian represents {{IPAchar|[ɛ]}} exclusively by ⟨{{l|frr|ä}}⟩, whereas the insular dialects represent {{IPAchar|[ə]}} by ⟨{{l|frr|i}}⟩ in certain positions (see there).
* Föhr-Amrum Frisian uses ⟨{{l|frr||ei, eu}}⟩ for the diphthongs {{IPAchar|[aɪ̯]}}, {{IPAchar|[ɔɪ̯]}} as in German. The other dialects spell phonetically ⟨{{l|frr||ai, oi}}⟩.

