=====Usage notes=====
This pronoun form is known from Valdres, Hallingdal, Numedal, parts of Telemark, Sunnmøre, Agder and Sogn, and also from Bardu and Målselv. In the Middle Norway it is used in two areas: east (Selbu and Tydal) and south-west (Meldal, Rennebu, Støren, Oppdal, Kvikne, Surnadal, Tingvoll and Tustna), while in areas of Svorkmo, Haltdal and Folldal being mixed from house to house.

Besides ''e'', in the southernmost part of Trøndelag there are used {{m|nn|je}} (Røros and Singsås) and, rarely, {{m|nn|ei}}. The closer you get to Trondheim, {{m|nn|æ}} and {{m|nn|æg}} are getting more common. Exterior areas like Snåsa, Lierne, Romsdal and Sunndal are using {{m|nn|i}}, but in the northernmost areas (Overhalla, Grong, Namsskogan and Røyrvik) the form {{m|nn|eig}} is used.

